    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137-a1">

                <pb facs="0235" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg155"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Informal Statement</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-17">December 17, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This Government does not question the right of the Japanese Government to make a
                    proposed increase in the submarine category in excess of the tonnage specified
                    in the London Naval Treaty, 1930, as not to be exceeded on December 31, 1936,
                    nor the right of the Japanese Government to be the sole judge in determining
                    whether its security has been affected to such an extent that the retention of
                    this excess tonnage in the submarine category becomes a necessity, on the
                    condition that the Japanese Government has recourse to Article 21 of the Treaty
                    which is the only method provided by the Treaty for raising the tonnage limits
                    of the Treaty.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
